}cc/build_engine/README.md:23:The image contains only the seven requested tools in `/app`, their generated shared libraries and the OpenMP runtime, on top of the CUDA runtime base. It has no compiler, source checkout, or weights. Its entrypoint is cleared, so invoke tools by full path, for example `/app/llama-bench`. Release/shared CUDA compilation uses the flags in `build-record.json`; CPU-native tuning, tests, downloaded UI, and OpenSSL are disabled. `LLAMA_CURL=OFF` is passed as requested, although this checkout treats LLAMA_CURL as deprecated. Source and patch identity are recorded as image labels; binaries' built-in Git version may say `unknown` because `.git` is not staged.
cc/build_engine/README.md:27:`build-record.json` uses schema version 1 for amd64 and version 2 for Jetson. It records status, failure stage/error, requested and resolved commit, Git tree ID and dirty status, patch SHA256 or null, tag/platform, recipe SHA256 and sizes, base references/digests, Docker and Buildx versions, CMake flags, Buildx metadata, image config ID/RepoDigests/Created/Architecture/Os, tool SHA256 values, saved archive SHA256/bytes, build duration and total duration. Fields remain null or empty when a failure occurs before collection. `build_wall_seconds` measures the Bake invocation, including export; `wall_seconds` covers the whole attempt.
